 simple='India has one unified court system: Supreme Court at the top, then High Courts, then Subordinate Courts, and the same courts apply Union and State laws. Judges must decide without pressure from Parliament or the government, because the government is the biggest litigant and courts guard the Constitution and rights. The Constitution gives tenure, salary, removal and other safeguards, yet appointments, the CJI\'s roster power, post-retirement jobs and funding still threaten independence. Independence is never freedom from accountability.',
