   '<b>2. Government as a major litigant:</b> the government is involved in a large number of cases. Independence ensures that judgments are not influenced by the government against which cases are filed.',
   '<b>3. Upholding the Constitution:</b> courts must protect the Constitution from unconstitutional actions and laws enacted by the legislature or executive.',
   '<b>4. Preservation of Rule of Law:</b> members of the legislature and executive are not above the law. An independent judiciary ensures that the same law applies to everyone.',
   '<b>5. Protection of Fundamental Rights:</b> most writ petitions are complaints against government actions. Independence is necessary to protect citizens from arbitrary State action.',
