    ['Security of tenure', 'Supreme Court judges retire at <b>65 years</b> and High Court judges at <b>62 years</b>.'],
    ['Difficult removal process', 'Under <b>Articles 124(4) and 217</b>, judges can be removed only for <b>proved misbehaviour or incapacity</b>, following the prescribed special-majority parliamentary procedure.'],
    ['Financial security', 'Supreme Court judges\' salaries are charged to the <b>Consolidated Fund of India</b>. High Court judges\' salaries are charged to the <b>Consolidated Fund of the State</b>, while their pensions are charged to the Consolidated Fund of India.'],
    ['Protection of service conditions', 'Judicial allowances and specified service benefits cannot be varied to a judge\'s disadvantage after appointment, subject to constitutional provisions.'],
